#### UI0; adding a screen ####################################################

In UI zero we display an arrow on each screen that can be used to navigate
between different elements of the interface. The menu of different screens
looks like this:

[ ![](images/ui0-menu-350x362.jpg "ui0 menu") ](images/ui0-menu.jpg)

To add a new screen to the UI and the menu, take these steps:

- in `unPhoneUI0.h`:
  - add a new member of the UI modes enumeration: `enum ui_modes_t { ...,
    ui_mynewelement, ... }`
  - declare a subclass of `UIElement`, e.g. `class MyNewUIElement: public
    UIElement { ...`
- in `unPhoneUI0.cpp`:
  - increase `NUM_UI_ELEMENTS` by one
  - add a name for the element to `ui_mode_names`, e.g. "My new UI screen" and
    add this to `modeName()`, e.g. `case ui_mynewelement: return
    "ui_mynewelement"; break;`
  - allocate storage for your element in `allocateUIElement()`, e.g. `case
    ui_testrig: m_element = new MyNewUIElement(up->tftp, up->tsp, up->sdp);
    break;`
  - implement the  methods of the new `UIElement` subclass, e.g. `void
    MyNewUIElement::draw() { ...;`

This should now appear on the UI zero menu screen. (For a detailed example,
see [this commit](
